2026-10-31T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A narrow unit holds a wide number as a sum of parts
 # uuid: 4497d8cf-00be-5a57-8e1b-e2f17125142e
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l2, rfd:attest-in:details
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-10-31T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2357) 'numeric precision for kernels on float32 and bf16 units
 # tags: rfd:feature
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2357) 'df32 guest geometry, and f32 matrix products on bf16 units such as a TPU.
 # tags: rfd:scope
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A narrow unit gives wide precision when each number is split into parts it can hold.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A float32 coordinate 3.8e8 m from the origin cannot hold a 1 mm step, and a bf16 unit holds 8
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2357) 'bits of mantissa.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2357) 'Record the measured error of a kernel before it claims float32 or df32 accuracy.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A narrow unit holds a wide number as a sum of parts
 # tags: rfd:details-title
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A TPU computes a float32 product as 3 or 6 bf16 passes. A df32 pair computes a wide
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2357) 'coordinate as a high and a low float32. Both split a number into a sum of narrow parts.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2357) '1. A kernel that needs more precision than its unit holds splits the operands into parts
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2357) '   and sums the products of the parts, smallest first.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2357) '2. A kernel states its part count: 1, 2 or 3 bf16 parts, or one df32 pair.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2357) '3. Each part count carries a measured error against a float64 reference, and a control
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2357) '   that fails when the count drops by one.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2357) 'RFD66606-2392 chooses df32 for guest geometry. RFD66606-1025 gives the bf16 memory
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2357) 'arithmetic. The BLOCKLIST row on XLA and PJRT keeps the Cloud TPU route open.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2357) 'What the TPU library states
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The array library that drives Cloud TPU documents its matrix precision setting in its
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2357) 'source, read from the main branch at the time of writing. The setting changes
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2357) 'float32 computations only and leaves the input and output types alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2357) '- `DEFAULT`: on TPU, float32 computations run in bfloat16.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2357) '- `HIGH`: on TPU, float32 computations run in 3 bfloat16 passes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2357) '- `HIGHEST`: on TPU, float32 computations run in 6 bfloat16 passes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The dot algorithm presets name the same idea: `BF16_BF16_F32_X3`, `BF16_BF16_F32_X6` and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2357) '`BF16_BF16_F32_X9` use 3, 6 and 9 operations to emulate higher precision, and a float8
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2357) 'preset decomposes each operand into an initial term and a residual term.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The source does not state which products the 3 and 6 pass modes keep, and no TPU ran
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2357) 'for this RFD. The host measurement below chooses the usual split: 2 parts keep the 3
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2357) 'products whose part indexes sum to at most 1, 3 parts keep the 6 whose indexes sum to at
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2357) 'most 2, and 9 keeps all products of 3 parts.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The split rule
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A part is the operand rounded to bf16. The residual is the operand minus the part, exact in
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2357) 'float32. The next part is the residual rounded to bf16, and so on. Three bf16 parts hold
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2357) '3 times 8 bits, which covers the 24 bit float32 mantissa.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A product of two bf16 values is exact in float32. The sum of the kept products runs in
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2357) 'float32, smallest products first, so the large products do not drown the small ones.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2357) 'df32 is the same split one level up. The high part is the float32 value and the low part
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2357) 'is the float32 residual of a float64. `two_sum`, `quick_two_sum` and `two_prod` carry the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2357) 'rounding error of each operation into the low part, as RFD66606-2392 lists.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2357) 'Measured on the host
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2357) 'A host emulation, not a TPU. Matrices 64 by K times K by 64, standard normal entries, 8
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2357) 'seeds. Error is the norm of the difference from a float64 product, over the norm of that
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2357) 'product. Median over the seeds, with the maximum in brackets.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2357) '| product                    | K = 256              | K = 4096             |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2357) '| -------------------------- | -------------------- | -------------------- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2357) '| 1 bf16 part                | 2.3e-3 (2.4e-3)      | 2.4e-3 (2.4e-3)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2357) '| 3 products, 2 parts (X3)   | 4.4e-6 (4.6e-6)      | 4.4e-6 (4.6e-6)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2357) '| 6 products, 3 parts (X6)   | 9.6e-8 (9.9e-8)      | 1.2e-7 (1.2e-7)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2357) '| 9 products, 3 parts (X9)   | 9.6e-8 (9.9e-8)      | 1.2e-7 (1.2e-7)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2357) '| float32 host product       | 2.5e-7 (2.6e-7)      | 2.4e-7 (2.4e-7)      |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2357) 'Each step up the table lowers the error, from 2.3e-3 to 1.2e-7 over three steps. The 3 part
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2357) 'products sit at the float32 rounding floor of 1.2e-7 (the float32 epsilon), and the ninth
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2357) 'product adds nothing over the sixth here. The host float32 product is a blocked product with
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2357) 'its own rounding, so a TPU accumulator can differ from every row.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2357) 'Control: the 1 bf16 part row is 520 times above the 2 part row, so a bound of 1e-5 fails a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2357) 'kernel that dropped to 1 part and passes the X3 row.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2357) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

