 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2357) 'The bf16 round is round to nearest even on the upper 16 bits of a float32. Parts come from
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2357) 'the residual rule above. Products and sums ran in float32 on the host with numpy. The df32
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2357) 'steps use `two_sum` and `quick_two_sum` on float32 scalars. The numbers above are the output
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2357) 'of a short script that is not committed; the kernels that RFD66606-2392 lists are the place
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2357) 'for a permanent gate.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2357  1 LINE
 Text:Written

